{"id":"3aa71857-2134-4e6d-8043-8022203c9591","object":"chat.completion","created":1785008683,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"attempts\\\" not in case or \\\"max_attempts\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must contain 'attempts' and 'max_attempts'\\\")\\n    attempts = case[\\\"attempts\\\"]\\n    max_attempts = case[\\\"max_attempts\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(attempts, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"attempts must be a list\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(max_attempts, int) or max_attempts < 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"max_attempts must be positive integer\\\")\\n    for i, att in enumerate(attempts):\\n        if not isinstance(att, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"attempt {i} must be a dict\\\")\\n        if \\\"success\\\" not in att or \\\"failure_signature\\\" not in att or \\\"reflection\\\" not in att:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"attempt {i} missing required keys\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(att[\\\"success\\\"], bool):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"attempt {i} success must be bool\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(att[\\\"failure_signature\\\"], str):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"attempt {i} failure_signature must be string\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(att[\\\"reflection\\\"], str):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"attempt {i} reflection must be string\\\")\\n    current_num = len(attempts)\\n    # Check success\\n    for att in attempts:\\n        if att[\\\"success\\\"]:\\n            return {\\\"decision\\\": \\\"stop\\\", \\\"memory_append\\\": None, \\\"next_attempt\\\": current_num}\\n    # Check budget exhaustion\\n    if current_num >= max_attempts:\\n        return {\\\"decision\\\": \\\"stop\\\", \\\"memory_append\\\": None, \\\"next_attempt\\\": current_num}\\n    # Check repeated failure signature among failed attempts\\n    failed_signatures = [att[\\\"failure_signature\\\"] for att in attempts if not att[\\\"success\\\"]]\\n    if len(failed_signatures) != len(set(failed_signatures)):\\n        return {\\\"decision\\\": \\\"stop\\\", \\\"memory_append\\\": None, \\\"next_attempt\\\": current_num}\\n    # Otherwise retry\\n    if current_num == 0:\\n        return {\\\"decision\\\": \\\"retry\\\", \\\"memory_append\\\": None, \\\"next_attempt\\\": 0}\\n    last = attempts[-1]\\n    reflection = last[\\\"reflection\\\"]\\n    signature = last[\\\"failure_signature\\\"]\\n    if not reflection:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"last attempt reflection must be nonempty\\\")\\n    memory_append = {\\\"reflection\\\": reflection, \\\"signature\\\": signature}\\n    return {\\\"decision\\\": \\\"retry\\\", \\\"memory_append\\\": memory_append, \\\"next_attempt\\\": current_num}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write Python code for solve(case) that implements the logic described. The task is AGENT-RF-02. Based on the fixture payload, the case contains: \"attempts\" (list of objects with success, failure_signature, reflection), and \"max_attempts\" (integer). Also \"_case_nonce\" but probably not needed.\n\nThe output schema: decision (string), memory_append (null or object with reflection and signature), next_attempt (integer).\n\nWe need to implement a \"trial_reflect_retry_controller\". From description: \"With no prior attempt request attempt one. Stop immediately after success. Stop on the registered attempt budget or a repeated failure signature. Otherwise request exactly the next attempt. Append a nonempty reflection with its signature and return decision, next index, and memory update.\"\n\nInterpretation: The case has attempts that have already been made? Actually fixture shows three attempts with success/failure. The controller is supposed to decide what to do next given the history of attempts. The case payload includes attempts array which are previous attempts. The agent must evaluate the current state: if any attempt succeeded, stop with decision \"success\"? Or if max_attempts reached? Or if repeated failure signature? If none, then request next attempt.\n\nThe description says \"Stop immediately after success.\" So if the last attempt (or any?) succeeded, we should return decision \"success\"? But the output schema has decision as string. We need to decide what values are allowed. Possibly \"stop\", \"continue\", \"success\", \"failure\"? Not specified. But from context: decision could be \"stop\" when we stop due to success or budget or repeated signature. Or maybe \"retry\" for next attempt. We need to infer.\n\nLook at the output schema: decision is type string, no enum. The task says \"Return decision, next index, and memory update.\" The memory_append is either null or object with reflection and signature. That suggests if we are stopping, we might return null for memory_append? Or if we are going to retry, we need to append a reflection from the last attempt? Actually the problem says \"Append a nonempty reflection with its signature\". Likely the memory_append should contain the reflection and signature from the most recent failed attempt? Or from the attempt that is being considered? Need to examine.\n\nThe fixture shows attempts with reflections like \"adjust-0\", \"adjust-1\", etc. The memory_append probably is the reflection from the latest attempt that we are using? Or if we stop, we don't append? In the output schema, memory_append can be null or object. So likely when we stop we set memory_append: null; when we continue (retry) we set it to contain the reflection and signature from the last attempt that triggered the retry? Or from the attempt that we are adding as part of controller? But the controller is not adding attempts; it's just processing existing attempts. Maybe it's about recording the last attempt's reflection into memory. The signature is a failure signature? The attempts have failure_signature only when success false. So reflection is presumably the agent's reflection on the failure.\n\nThe problem says: \"With no prior attempt request attempt one.\" So initial state: no attempts. In the case, there are prior attempts provided. So the function should evaluate the given attempts and decide what to do. It should also consider max_attempts. It should stop on repeated failure signature: if any failure signature repeats (maybe the same as a previous failure signature), then stop.\n\nAlso \"Stop on the registered attempt budget\": if number of attempts already made equals max_attempts, stop.\n\n\"Otherwise request exactly the next attempt.\" That means decision should indicate \"retry\" or \"continue\"? And next_attempt should be the next index (probably 0-indexed count of attempts? The output next_attempt is integer. The fixture shows attempts indices: 0,1,2. So next_attempt would be 3 if continuing. If stopping, next_attempt might be the number of attempts? Or maybe always the next attempt number? But if stopping, next_attempt might be the current index? Not sure.\n\nWe need to derive from expected outputs. Since no expected outputs are given, we must infer from the logic.\n\nGiven the fixture payloads: \n- Case 000: attempts: three, last success true. max_attempts=4. Should stop due to success. So decision likely \"success\" or \"stop\". next_attempt? maybe 3? But we don't need to continue. memory_append: null (since success).\n- Case 001: attempts: four, all failures, max_attempts=4. Last attempt failure signature e0 (repeated from first attempt? first attempt also e0). So repeated failure signature? Yes, e0 appears twice (attempts[0] and attempts[3]). So should stop due to repeated signature. Also budget used exactly max_attempts. So decision \"stop\", next_attempt? maybe 4 (since that is count). memory_append: null.\n- Case 002: attempts: three, all failures, max_attempts=4. No success, no repeated signature (e0, e1, e2 are distinct), budget not exhausted. So should request next attempt. decision \"retry\" or \"continue\"? next_attempt = 3 (since 3 attempts done, next index 3). memory_append: should contain reflection and signature from last attempt (attempts[2] with reflection \"adjust-2\" and failure_signature \"e2\").\n\nThus we can define decision values: \"stop\" (or \"success\"? But even non-success stop could be \"stop\") and \"retry\". But we need a single string. The output schema only says string. Let's use \"stop\" for termination, \"retry\" for continue. The problem says \"return decision, next index, and memory update.\" So decision should indicate the action.\n\nNow we need to implement solve(case). The case is a dict with keys: \"attempts\", \"max_attempts\", maybe \"_case_nonce\". Must validate required fields. If missing, raise ValueError.\n\nProcedure:\n- Extract attempts list and max_attempts. attempts must be list of dicts each with success, failure_signature, reflection.\n- Compute current number of attempts: len(attempts).\n- Check for success: if any attempt success==True, decision=\"stop\", memory_append=None, next_attempt = current number? Actually if we stop, next_attempt could be the index of next attempt (which would be current count) but it doesn't matter. The output schema requires next_attempt integer. Could set to current count (len(attempts)). That seems consistent: next attempt index that would have been tried.\n- Else, check if number of attempts >= max_attempts: if yes, stop (budget exhausted): decision=\"stop\", memory_append=None, next_attempt = len(attempts).\n- Else, check repeated failure signature. We need to check if any failure signature appears more than once among failed attempts? The description: \"Stop on the registered attempt budget or a repeated failure signature.\" So if any failure signature occurs more than once (i.e., duplicate), stop. We should consider only failed attempts? The success attempts might also have failure_signature? In the fixtures, success attempts have failure_signature but it's a dummy? Actually in the fixture, the success attempt still has failure_signature: \"e2\" but success true. So we need to decide: treat success as not a failure. But repeated failure signature probably refers to failures. The third attempt in case 000 succeeded, but its failure_signature is \"e2\". That doesn't cause a repeat because it's success. In case 001, first and fourth both have failure_signature \"e0\" and both failed. So check only among attempts where success==False. Collect failure_signatures of failed attempts. If any signature appears more than once, stop.\n- If none of above, decision=\"retry\", next_attempt = len(attempts) (index of next attempt). memory_append = {\"reflection\": last attempt's reflection, \"signature\": last attempt's failure_signature}. The last attempt is the most recent attempt (attempts[-1]). If that attempt failed, it's fine. If succeeded? But we already checked success earlier, so if we are here, the last attempt must have failed. But to be safe, we can take the reflection and signature from the last attempt (which is failed because we didn't exit due to success). However if the case has mixed success and failures? The logic says stop immediately after success, so if any earlier attempt succeeded, we would have stopped earlier. So the last attempt must be failed.\n\nEdge case: if attempts list empty? Then we need to request first attempt. decision=\"retry\", next_attempt=0, memory_append? With no prior attempt, what memory? Possibly null? The problem says \"With no prior attempt request attempt one.\" So no reflection to append? But the output schema says memory_append can be null. So when no prior attempt, we set memory_append=None. But we need to check: The case payload may have empty attempts? The fixture doesn't show. We'll handle.\n\nAlso need to ensure reflection is nonempty. The fixture has \"adjust-0\" etc, nonempty. If a reflection is empty string, maybe raise ValueError? The problem says \"nonempty reflection\". So if we need to include a reflection from last attempt and it's empty, that could be invalid. But we trust input? The function should validate: if we need to append reflection, it must be nonempty string; otherwise raise ValueError? The instruction: \"Validate every required field before computing a result.\" So check that attempts list items have required keys and types. For reflection, if we need to output it, it must be nonempty. Similarly signature nonempty? Not explicitly but likely.\n\nWe'll implement with validation: check attempts is list, each element is dict with required keys: success (bool), failure_signature (string), reflection (string). Also max_attempts is int >= 1? Probably.\n\nNow implement solve(case) returning dict with keys: decision, memory_append, next_attempt.\n\nMemory_append: null if stop or no prior attempt, else object with reflection and signature.\n\nNote: The output schema says memory_append can be null or object with required fields reflection and signature. So we need to match exactly.\n\nNow write Python code with proper validation.\n\nWe'll not mutate case.\n\nNow produce the final JSON with \"implementation\" key containing the Python source as a string.\n\nMake sure to escape newlines and quotes.\n\nLet's write the code:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate input structure\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    if \"attempts\" not in case or \"max_attempts\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"case must contain 'attempts' and 'max_attempts'\")\n    attempts = case[\"attempts\"]\n    max_attempts = case[\"max_attempts\"]\n    if not isinstance(attempts, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"attempts must be a list\")\n    if not isinstance(max_attempts, int) or max_attempts < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"max_attempts must be positive integer\")\n    for i, att in enumerate(attempts):\n        if not isinstance(att, dict):\n            raise ValueError(f\"attempt {i} must be a dict\")\n        if \"success\" not in att or \"failure_signature\" not in att or \"reflection\" not in att:\n            raise ValueError(f\"attempt {i} missing required keys\")\n        if not isinstance(att[\"success\"], bool):\n            raise ValueError(f\"attempt {i} success must be bool\")\n        if not isinstance(att[\"failure_signature\"], str):\n            raise ValueError(f\"attempt {i} failure_signature must be string\")\n        if not isinstance(att[\"reflection\"], str):\n            raise ValueError(f\"attempt {i} reflection must be string\")\n    current_num = len(attempts)\n    # Check success\n    for att in attempts:\n        if att[\"success\"]:\n            # Stop due to success\n            return {\"decision\": \"stop\", \"memory_append\": None, \"next_attempt\": current_num}\n    # Check budget exhaustion\n    if current_num >= max_attempts:\n        return {\"decision\": \"stop\", \"memory_append\": None, \"next_attempt\": current_num}\n    # Check repeated failure signature among failed attempts\n    failed_signatures = [att[\"failure_signature\"] for att in attempts if not att[\"success\"]]\n    if len(failed_signatures) != len(set(failed_signatures)):\n        # duplicate found\n        return {\"decision\": \"stop\", \"memory_append\": None, \"next_attempt\": current_num}\n    # Otherwise retry\n    # No prior attempt case\n    if current_num == 0:\n        return {\"decision\": \"retry\", \"memory_append\": None, \"next_attempt\": 0}\n    # Append memory from last attempt (must be failed because we already checked success)\n    last = attempts[-1]\n    reflection = last[\"reflection\"]\n    signature = last[\"failure_signature\"]\n    if not reflection:\n        raise ValueError(\"last attempt reflection must be nonempty\")\n    memory_append = {\"reflection\": reflection, \"signature\": signature}\n    return {\"decision\": \"retry\", \"memory_append\": memory_append, \"next_attempt\": current_num}\n```\n\nBut note: In the case of retry with no prior attempt, we set next_attempt=0 (first attempt). That matches \"request attempt one\".\n\nNow ensure that we return next_attempt as integer. Output schema expects integer.\n\nNow we need to produce JSON with implementation string.\n\nWe'll output:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ... \\n\"}\n\nMake sure to escape properly.\n\nNow produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1440,"completion_tokens":3635,"total_tokens":5075,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1408},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2960},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1408,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":32},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}